Subject: [PATCH 2/5] server: critic_thread_gate.py, the DAR-LAT-3h gate G1
 driver (PROPOSED)

Measures three launch arms of the production :8074 argv on port 18074:
L (-t 96, live env), R96 (-t 96 + recipe GGML knobs), R48 (-t 48 + recipe
knobs = the full codified recipe). 12 launches, 4 per arm, balanced blocks.
Workloads: W1 the 24-prompt production mix (champion harness shape), W2 a
~4k-token critique shape, W3 a frontdoor :8070 co-run probe.

The pre-registered rule (decide) picks R48, else R96, else L, on wall time
(the critic's region-lock hold time, i.e. frontdoor's cost of a consult),
TTFT and coherence. It kills only the PIDs it spawns and verifies each is
dead. INERT: nothing imports it; it is run by the inference owner after the
operator signs.

